      "description": "US Water Systems is an unsupported repository umbrella for two separate municipal water and wastewater concession investments: the Bayonne water and wastewater concession in New Jersey and Middletown Water Joint Venture LLC in Pennsylvania. SUEZ and New York regulatory materials describe the concessions separately, and Water Capital Partners' current project list does the same; no reviewed source identifies a legal US Water Systems entity or one operating platform above both investments. Argo acquired KKR and SUEZ interests in the two concession SPVs in 2017, while Veolia/SUEZ remained the operator and minority participant. Current municipal, operator and project records show both concessions remain active. Apollo's announced acquisition of the Argo manager did not close and was terminated in January 2026, so Apollo never became an owner of the assets. This umbrella record is archived from the manager-level PortCo census without a redirect to prevent double counting; the separate Bayonne and Middletown records remain published. No later sale, concession termination, signed pending exit or ownership transfer was identified through August 16, 2026.",
